  "steps": [
    "Rinse the red lentils under cold water until the water runs mostly clear.",
    "Heat the vegetable oil in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until softened and lightly golden.",
    "Add the garlic, chilli, ground cumin and turmeric. Cook for 30 to 60 seconds until fragrant.",
    "Stir in the canned tomatoes, red lentils, water and salt. Bring to a boil, then reduce to a gentle simmer.",
    "Cook for 18 to 22 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the lentils are soft and the dal has thickened. Add a splash more water if it becomes too thick.",
    "Stir in the lemon juice. Taste and adjust the salt.",
    "Serve hot, finished with fresh coriander on top."
  ],
